<title>UK: CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP CLOSES.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP CLOSES.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Close of play scores on the third</p>
<p>day of four-day English County Championship cricket matches on</p>
<p>Friday:</p>
<p>At Chester-le-Street: Durham v Hampshire - no play due to</p>
<p>rain.</p>
<p>At Chelmsford: Essex 280 (D.Robinson 78, P.Prichard 51;</p>
<p>J.Kerr 4-83) &amp; 129 (S.Law 55; K.Shine 5-72). Somerset 389</p>
<p>(P.Holloway 90, M.Lathwell 87, R.Turner 80 not out) &amp; 22-0.</p>
<p>Somerset beat Essex by 10 wickets</p>
<p>At Swansea: Glamorgan 400-5 declared (H.Morris 173, M.Maynard</p>
<p>98, P.Cottey 76 not out) v Gloucestershire 214 &amp; 54-1.</p>
<p>At Maidstone: Kent 306 (N.Llong 57, P.Strang 55; M Akram</p>
<p>4-56) &amp; 99-2 declared v Northamptonshire 84-0 declared.</p>
<p>At Leicester: Yorkshire 268 (D. Byas 88; A.Mullally 5-103) v</p>
<p>Leicestershire 363-6 (D.Maddy 94, J.Whitaker 87).</p>
<p>At Uxbridge: Middlesex 118 (P.Martin 8-32) &amp; 198-6 (J.Kallis</p>
<p>62) v Lancashire 417-9 declared (N.Fairbrother 97, S.Titchard</p>
<p>79, N. Wood 67; P.Tufnell 5-90).</p>
<p>At Arundel: Worcestershire 255 (S.Rhodes 58 not out) v Sussex</p>
<p>71 (A.Sheriyar 6-19) &amp; 149 (S.Lampitt 5-39, A.Sheriyar 4-44).</p>
<p>Worcestershire beat Sussex by an innings and 35 runs</p>
<p>At Edgbaston: Surrey 193 (G.Welch 4-62, A.Donald 4-64) &amp; 144</p>
<p>(J.Radcliffe 59; A.Donald 6-55) v Warwickshire 306 (D.Brown 66,</p>
<p>N.Smith 69 not out) &amp; 23-4.</p>
</text>
